00:54:21.220 --> 00:54:24.760
And then really loudly into the microphone, Meg Ryan goes, Helen.
接着梅格·瑞恩非常大声地对着麦克风喊道，海伦。

1257
00:54:25.780 --> 00:54:27.820
And it like goes out over the store.
声音就这么传遍了整个商店。

1258
00:54:28.000 --> 00:54:30.620
I always thought that was such a funny bit.
我一直觉得这个桥段太搞笑了。

1259
00:54:30.800 --> 00:54:34.900
So I thought I'm going to say I'm sorry into the mic really loudly.
所以我想我要对着麦克风很大声地说我很抱歉。

1260
00:54:36.000 --> 00:54:37.200
And I don't know.
而且我不知道。

1261
00:54:37.720 --> 00:54:42.200
I mean, probably no one would ever think about it.
我的意思是，可能根本没人会去想这件事。

1262
00:54:42.380 --> 00:54:44.800
But about your inspiration for that moment.
但关于你创作那个时刻的灵感。

1263
00:54:45.000 --> 00:54:45.680
I love that.
我太喜欢了。

1264
00:54:45.780 --> 00:54:46.680
I think that's so sweet.
我觉得这太贴心了。

1265
00:54:46.820 --> 00:54:49.860
I also know how much you love When Harry Met Sally.
我也知道你有多喜欢《当哈利遇到莎莉》。

1266
00:54:49.860 --> 00:54:51.280
It's one of your favorite movies.
那是你最喜欢的电影之一。

1267
00:54:51.720 --> 00:54:58.060
Lady, when I was in college, I had a three and a half hour drive between St. Louis, which
天哪，我上大学的时候，从圣路易斯——

1268
00:54:58.060 --> 00:55:04.880
is where my parents still lived, and Kirksville, Missouri, which is a little rural town in Missouri
也就是我父母当时住的地方，到密苏里州的柯克斯维尔，车程要三个半小时，那是密苏里州的一个小乡村城镇

1269
00:55:04.880 --> 00:55:07.700
where I went to college at Truman State University.
我在那里的杜鲁门州立大学上大学。

1270
00:55:08.200 --> 00:55:15.020
And what I did to pass the time was I recorded When Harry Met Sally onto an audio tape.
我打发时间的方法就是把《当哈利遇到莎莉》录在一盘磁带上。

1271
00:55:15.660 --> 00:55:22.000
And then I played the movie back for myself in my car on my drive.
然后我在开车的时候，在车里放这部电影给自己听。

1272
00:55:22.000 --> 00:55:26.140
I have that entire movie memorized from beginning to end.
那部电影我从头到尾都能背下来。

1273
00:55:26.700 --> 00:55:27.740
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

1274
00:55:28.000 --> 00:55:28.100
I love that.
我好喜欢这个。

1275
00:55:28.340 --> 00:55:30.020
That is the sweetest thing.
这简直是太甜了。

1276
00:55:30.260 --> 00:55:30.680
Yeah.
是啊。

1277
00:55:30.840 --> 00:55:36.000
I recorded on my tape recorder David Letterman's opening monologues.
我用我的录音机录下过大卫·莱特曼的开场独白。

1278
00:55:36.300 --> 00:55:40.020
And I would play them back and listen to his opening monologues.
然后我会放出来听他的开场独白。

1279
00:55:40.020 --> 00:55:41.680
Oh, my gosh.
噢，天哪。

1280
00:55:42.100 --> 00:55:46.260
Well, you said you wanted to work for a late night talk show.
好吧，你说过你想为深夜脱口秀工作。

1281
00:55:46.440 --> 00:55:47.640
I wanted to work in comedy.
我想从事喜剧工作。

1282
00:55:47.900 --> 00:55:50.180
You love, yeah, comedy, late night.
你喜欢，对，喜剧，深夜节目。

1283
00:55:50.500 --> 00:55:50.680
Yeah.
对。

1284
00:55:51.200 --> 00:55:51.300
Yeah.
是啊。

1285
00:55:52.040 --> 00:55:52.900
Aw, lady.
噢，天哪。

1286
00:55:53.260 --> 00:55:54.880
Look, we were meant to be BFFs.
听着，我们注定是要成为闺蜜的。

1287
00:55:54.940 --> 00:55:56.680
We were both driving in our cars.
我们俩当时都在车里开车。

1288
00:55:57.040 --> 00:55:57.400
We were.
确实是。

1289
00:55:57.520 --> 00:56:04.140
Listening to things we recorded off of our TVs because we're 100 on our tape decks.
用我们的磁带录音机听着我们从电视上录下来的东西。

1290
00:56:04.620 --> 00:56:06.680
Lady, I just got a text from Lee.
天哪，我刚收到李发来的短信。

1291
00:56:06.900 --> 00:56:08.040
He sent me a photo of-
他给我发了一张照片——

1292
00:56:08.040 --> 00:56:09.000
Is this about your bread?
这是关于你做的面包吗？

1293
00:56:09.000 --> 00:56:09.300
Yeah.
对。

1294
00:56:09.580 --> 00:56:10.960
Can I go down and check it out?
我能下去看看吗？

1295
00:56:11.040 --> 00:56:11.840
Can we take a break?
我们能休息一下吗？

1296
00:56:11.840 --> 00:56:13.580
He made sandwiches for the kids.
他给孩子们做了三明治。

1297
00:56:13.760 --> 00:56:15.020
I want to see if they like it.
我想看看他们喜不喜欢。

1298
00:56:15.100 --> 00:56:15.860
Oh, my God.
噢，天哪。

1299
00:56:15.860 --> 00:56:16.520
He did it.
他真的做成了。

1300
00:56:16.640 --> 00:56:17.260
Way to go, Lee.
干得漂亮，李。

1301
00:56:17.620 --> 00:56:18.700
But did they eat it?
但他们吃了吗？

1302
00:56:18.820 --> 00:56:19.700
That's the question.
这就是问题所在。

1303
00:56:19.700 --> 00:56:20.580
We'll find out.
我们马上揭晓。

1304
00:56:20.860 --> 00:56:21.120
All right.
好吧。

1305
00:56:21.180 --> 00:56:21.920
We'll be right back.
我们马上回来。

1306
00:56:32.550 --> 00:56:35.010
Bread report for everyone who's curious.
给所有好奇的人的吐司报告。

1307
00:56:35.810 --> 00:56:37.010
It's freaking delicious.
简直太好吃了。

1308
00:56:37.030 --> 00:56:38.110
I just ate a slice.
我刚吃了一片。

1309
00:56:38.370 --> 00:56:38.910
Is it?
是吗？

1310
00:56:39.110 --> 00:56:39.590
It's good.
很好吃。

1311
00:56:39.590 --> 00:56:41.170
I don't know if the kids are going to eat it.
我不知道孩子们会不会吃。

1312
00:56:41.250 --> 00:56:42.170
What is their deal?
他们是怎么回事？

1313
00:56:42.470 --> 00:56:43.290
You know what, Angela?
你知道吗，安吉拉？

1314
00:56:43.590 --> 00:56:45.750
They love all of my other breads.
他们喜欢我做的所有其他面包。

1315
00:56:45.890 --> 00:56:47.110
They love my sourdough bread.
他们喜欢我的酸面包。

1316
00:56:47.110 --> 00:56:48.330
They love when I make rolls.
他们喜欢我做的小面包卷。

1317
00:56:48.610 --> 00:56:49.870
They love when I make popovers.
他们喜欢我做的泡芙饼。

1318
00:56:49.870 --> 00:56:54.010
For whatever reason, I cannot get them to like my sandwich bread.
不管出于什么原因，我就是没办法让他们喜欢我的三明治面包。

1319
00:56:54.630 --> 00:56:57.110
They just want store-bought sandwich bread.
他们只想吃买来的三明治面包。

1320
00:56:57.270 --> 00:56:58.890
I've tried three different recipes.
我试过三个不同的食谱了。

1321
00:56:59.090 --> 00:57:01.590
Today will have been my third sandwich bread recipe.
今天已经是我做的第三个三明治面包食谱了。

1322
00:57:01.990 --> 00:57:02.910
I don't know.
我不知道。

1323
00:57:02.970 --> 00:57:08.270
Or they will like it the day it comes out of the oven, but the next day, it's a no-go for them.
或者他们会在出炉当天喜欢它，但第二天，他们就绝对不碰了。

1324
00:57:08.430 --> 00:57:10.550
They only want it warm out of the oven.
他们只想吃刚出炉热乎的。

1325
00:57:10.710 --> 00:57:11.330
I don't know.
我不知道。

1326
00:57:11.330 --> 00:57:14.270
Shall we get back into this episode, my lady?
我们要继续这一集吗，夫人？

1327
00:57:14.670 --> 00:57:15.990
I think we should.
我觉得我们应该继续。

1328
00:57:15.990 --> 00:57:17.110
Where are we?
我们讲到哪了？

1329
00:57:18.110 --> 00:57:24.530
I believe that we are back in human resources.
我记我们回到了人力资源部。

1330
00:57:25.130 --> 00:57:26.930
15 minutes, 15 seconds.
15分15秒。

1331
00:57:27.190 --> 00:57:30.330
Kevin is talking to Toby about his skin cancer.
凯文正在和托比谈论他的皮肤癌。

1332
00:57:30.750 --> 00:57:30.890
Yeah.
对。

1333
00:57:31.050 --> 00:57:35.470
And this is a nice callback to season one's healthcare episode because Toby's like,
这是一个对第一季医疗保健集的巧妙呼应，因为托比说，

1334
00:57:35.590 --> 00:57:37.870
can you get on your fiance's healthcare plan?
你能加入你未婚妻的医疗保险计划吗？

1335
00:57:37.990 --> 00:57:39.390
Because honestly, ours is horrible.
因为说实话，我们的太糟糕了。

1336
00:57:40.270 --> 00:57:41.070
That's right.
没错。

1337
00:57:41.270 --> 00:57:44.710
So to me, it was a nice callback to the healthcare episode.
所以对我来说，这是对医疗保健集的一个很好呼应。

1338
00:57:44.910 --> 00:57:50.250
Well, Michael comes over with a bunch of facts that are about why Kevin shouldn't be worried.
迈克尔走过来，带了一堆关于为什么凯文不该担心的事实。

1339
00:57:50.270 --> 00:57:51.690
He's got some statistics.
他带了一些统计数据。

1340
00:57:52.030 --> 00:57:58.390
The subtext is why we can still celebrate Michael's birthday without any problem,
其潜台词是，为什么我们仍然可以毫无问题地庆祝迈克尔的生日，

1341
00:57:58.390 --> 00:58:01.510
but he's presenting it as why Kevin shouldn't be worried.
但他把它表现为为什么凯文不应该担心。

1342
00:58:01.750 --> 00:58:01.950
Yeah.
对。

1343
00:58:02.490 --> 00:58:06.130
And then Toby's like, you know, kind of gives him some Toby sass.
然后托比就，你知道的，有点冲他发了点托比式的傲娇。

1344
00:58:06.310 --> 00:58:08.150
And Michael's like, why are you here?
迈克尔就说，你为什么在这里？

1345
00:58:08.650 --> 00:58:10.670
And Toby's like, I work here?
托比就说，我在这里上班啊？

1346
00:58:10.990 --> 00:58:16.830
Well, now Michael is going to announce that they're going somewhere and it's to make Kevin
好了，现在迈克尔要宣布他们要去一个地方，这是为了让凯文

1347
00:58:16.830 --> 00:58:17.510
feel better.
感觉好点。

1348
00:58:17.650 --> 00:58:19.530
There's an outing for the whole office.
全办公室要一起出去玩。

1349
00:58:19.730 --> 00:58:26.710
But of course, if you remember in an earlier scene, Michael asked Dwight if he's made all
但当然，如果你还记得前面的一幕，迈克尔问过德怀特是否已经为

1350
00:58:26.710 --> 00:58:27.830
the plans for later.
之后的活动做好了所有计划。

1351
00:58:28.030 --> 00:58:29.630
So this is clearly been in the works.
所以这显然是早有准备的。

1352
00:58:29.650 --> 00:58:30.310
Oh, there's a big banner when we walk in.
哦，我们走进去时挂着一条大横幅。

1353
00:58:30.350 --> 00:58:31.430
It says, happy birthday, Michael.
上面写着，迈克尔，生日快乐。

1354
00:58:31.430 --> 00:58:33.230
Like, this was planned for sure.
就好像，这绝对是计划好的。

1355
00:58:33.370 --> 00:58:35.850
Not by the party planning committee, by the way.
顺便说一句，可不是由派对策划委员会策划的。

1356
00:58:36.010 --> 00:58:38.210
Angela would not allocate funds to this.
安吉拉才不会给这事拨款呢。

1357
00:58:38.570 --> 00:58:40.050
But Dwight had this.
但德怀特把这事包了。

1358
00:58:40.190 --> 00:58:41.050
He had planned it.
这是他计划的。

1359
00:58:41.090 --> 00:58:46.670
We had a fan question from Noel, Angela, because we're about to go to the ice skating rink now.
安吉拉，我们收到了来自诺埃尔的粉丝提问，因为我们现在马上要去溜冰场了。

1360
00:58:47.190 --> 00:58:50.950
And that's the big surprise that he's taking us all ice skating.
这就是他带大家去溜冰的巨大惊喜。

1361
00:58:51.150 --> 00:58:55.690
And Noel wanted to know, did you have a safety meeting about ice skating?
诺埃尔想知道，你们开过关于溜冰的安全会议吗？

1362
00:58:56.210 --> 00:58:56.590
Remember?
记得吗？

1363
00:58:56.590 --> 00:58:58.550
Safety meeting lit candle.
安全会议，点燃的蜡烛。

1364
00:58:58.870 --> 00:59:00.050
I'm sure we did.
我确信我们开过。

1365
00:59:00.270 --> 00:59:06.090
I'm sure there was a safety meeting about we have heavy things being held on the ice.
我确信肯定开过安全会议，关于我们要在冰面上拿重物什么的。

1366
00:59:06.230 --> 00:59:08.490
I'm sure there was all kinds of safety meetings.
我确信有各种各样的安全会议。

1367
00:59:08.750 --> 00:59:10.750
Well, I know we had a medic there.
好吧，我知道我们在那儿有个医疗员。

1368
00:59:11.070 --> 00:59:16.990
And the reason that I know this is because, I don't know if you remember, Angela, but Mindy
我知道这一点的原因是，安吉拉，我不知道你记不记得，明迪

1369
00:59:16.990 --> 00:59:18.770
fell while we were shooting.
在拍摄时摔倒了。

1370
00:59:18.770 --> 00:59:19.790
I don't remember that.
我不记得了。

1371
00:59:19.810 --> 00:59:20.710
And she hurt her knee.
而且她伤了膝盖。

1372
00:59:20.890 --> 00:59:24.790
So you know there's that little bit at the ice skating rink where Kelly is helping Ryan?
所以你知道溜冰场里有那么一小段，凯莉在帮瑞恩吗？

1373
00:59:24.990 --> 00:59:25.210
Yeah.
对。

1374
00:59:25.210 --> 00:59:30.190
Well, she fell and she hurt her knee and the medic had to give her some ice, but she was
嗯，她摔倒了，膝盖受伤了，医疗员不得不给她一些冰块，但她

1375
00:59:30.190 --> 00:59:31.670
able to finish filming.
还是完成了拍摄。

1376
00:59:31.930 --> 00:59:32.810
Her knee was okay.
她的膝盖没事。

1377
00:59:33.090 --> 00:59:36.830
I thought it was interesting when you saw the different couplings of people ice skating.
我觉得看到人们在溜冰时不同的组合挺有意思的。

1378
00:59:36.990 --> 00:59:38.450
In the beginning, you see Kelly and Ryan.
一开始，你看到凯莉和瑞恩。

1379
00:59:38.770 --> 00:59:40.730
You see Pam and Jim.
你看到帕姆和吉姆。

1380
00:59:41.370 --> 00:59:43.470
I sort of just kind of go around solo.
我差不多就是自己一个人溜。

1381
00:59:43.490 --> 00:59:43.810
Yes.
是的。

1382
00:59:43.810 --> 00:59:44.370
So does Dwight.
德怀特也是。

1383
00:59:44.590 --> 00:59:47.610
We just kind of, we don't, you know, want anyone to know we're seeing each other.
我们只是，你知道的，不想让任何人知道我们在约会。

1384
00:59:47.690 --> 00:59:48.710
So we skate alone.
所以我们独自溜冰。

1385
00:59:48.710 --> 00:59:54.730
And then later, you see Ryan and Phyllis holding hands and ice skating.
然后后来，你看到瑞恩和菲利斯手拉手在溜冰。

1386
00:59:55.010 --> 00:59:55.490
Yes.
是的。

1387
00:59:55.610 --> 00:59:56.890
At 19 minutes.
在19分钟的时候。

1388
00:59:57.450 --> 01:00:03.210
We had a fan catch by KP who said, I love when you see Ryan and Phyllis at the skating
我们收到了KP的一个粉丝抓包，他说，我喜欢看你在溜冰场看到瑞恩和菲利斯手拉手，这样瑞恩就不会摔倒。

1389
01:00:03.210 --> 01:00:05.110
rink holding hands so Ryan won't fall.
这真是对他们友谊的一个随机一瞥。

1390
01:00:05.350 --> 01:00:07.710
It's such a random glimpse into their friendship.
安吉拉，我觉得他们那样做是因为明迪当时在给膝盖冰敷。

1391
01:00:07.710 --> 01:00:11.130
I think, Angela, they did that because Mindy was icing her knee.
如果你仔细看，真正可爱的是菲利斯乐坏了。

1392
01:00:11.330 --> 01:00:14.610
And what's really cute if you watch it is Phyllis is so tickled.
她高兴坏了。

1393
01:00:14.770 --> 01:00:15.890
She's so tickled.
真的非常可爱。

1394
01:00:15.970 --> 01:00:17.130
It's just really cute.
非常非常甜。

1395
01:00:17.330 --> 01:00:18.550
It's very, very sweet.
而且实际上，我看了那个评论后又回去看了一遍，看到他们俩一起溜冰真的

1396
01:00:18.630 --> 01:00:23.130
And I actually, I went back after I read that comment and I watched it and it's really very
非常甜美。

1397
01:00:23.130 --> 01:00:25.690
sweet to see the two of them skating together.
所以那是个意外。

1398
01:00:25.750 --> 01:00:27.790
So that was an accident.
我还有来自加利福尼亚的“超长寿”的一个粉丝提问。

1399
01:00:27.790 --> 01:00:31.230
I had another fan question from Live Long, California.
你和约翰本来就会溜冰，还是为了这一集不得不学？

1400
01:00:31.510 --> 01:00:36.970
Did you and John know how to ice skate or did you have to learn for this episode?
你和约翰本来就会溜冰，还是为了这一集不得不学？

1401
01:00:37.210 --> 01:00:38.870
So here's something interesting.
所以这里有个有趣的事。

1402
01:00:39.130 --> 01:00:42.670
In this episode, Jim is kind of helping Pam on the ice.
在这集里，吉姆算是帮了帕姆一把。

1403
01:00:43.170 --> 01:00:49.450
But right before we filmed this episode, I had actually been in some intense ice skating
但就在我们拍摄这一集之前，我其实刚进行过高强度的滑冰

1404
01:00:49.450 --> 01:00:53.370
training because I was filming a movie with Will Ferrell called Blades of Glory.
训练，因为我当时在和威尔·法瑞尔拍一部名叫《冰刀双人组》的电影。

1405
01:00:54.590 --> 01:01:00.050
And yeah, every Saturday morning for a few months, I had to go early in the morning and
没错，连续几个月的每个周六早晨，我都得起个大早去

1406
01:01:00.050 --> 01:01:01.730
spend about three hours learning to ice skate.
花大约三个小时学习滑冰。

1407
01:01:01.870 --> 01:01:05.930
And the crazy thing is my character didn't even ice skate in the movie.
最疯狂的是，我的角色在电影里根本不用滑冰。

1408
01:01:06.170 --> 01:01:12.330
I am completely pretending to not know how to ice skate in this scene on The Office because
